# Cold-start the issue-flow harness

Run this when a project needs the issue-flow scaffold, or when a **parent folder of related git repos** needs `issue-flow workspace bootstrap`. This is the slash/skill counterpart of the CLI's `issue-flow init` — **not** the step that pulls a GitHub issue into `{{ issueflows_dir }}/`. Use **`/iflow-capture`** for that.

`/iflow-init` is **off-path**: `/iflow` never auto-dispatches here. A user-global copy of this skill is installed on `init` / `update` so the command works before a project scaffold exists.

{% include "skills/_model_directive.md.j2" %}

## Input

Optional free-form text (editor id, `--force` intent, parent-folder hint). Prefer explicit confirm before any `issue-flow init --force` or `workspace bootstrap --yes`.

## Steps

1. **Start dir** = `root:` / `-C` / cwd. If this looks like a **parent folder of repos**, do **not** `agent resolve` first (it may pick a default member).

2. **Workspace file already there** — offer `workspace update` / per-member `update`. No re-bootstrap unless the user asks `--force`.

3. **Classify** — `issue-flow workspace bootstrap <start> --json`. Two or more own-git children (`scaffolded` / `unscaffolded`): show the list, propose `--default`, run `--yes` only after confirm. Then `/iflow-pick` per repo. Non-git folders → `/iflow-setup`. Never `git init` children; never write `{{ issueflows_dir }}/` on the parent.

4. **Single project, missing scaffold** — show `issue-flow init .` (or `uvx issue-flow init .`). Offer to run it only after yes. After success, `/iflow-pick` or `/iflow-capture <N>`.

5. **Single project, already present** — `issue-flow update .`, `/iflow-doctor` for missing editors, **`/iflow-capture`**, `/iflow-pick`. No `init --force` unless explicitly requested.

6. **Report** — workspace vs single-project, what ran, next step.

## Constraints

- Off-path; never auto-dispatched by `/iflow`.
- Never capture a GitHub issue or write `issue<N>_*.md` from this command.
- Never invent a second scaffolder; never force-reinit without explicit ask.

## Example invocations

- `/iflow-init` — check / cold-start the harness
- `/iflow-init` (parent folder of git siblings) — classify, then `workspace bootstrap --yes`
- `/iflow-init` (after clone, no `.issueflows/`) — guide `issue-flow init .`
